WEBVTT

00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:02.359
Open My certifications in Responder.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.989
This area gives the signed-in member a place to review their

00:00:06.019 --> 00:00:07.630
own certification records.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.270
The training account has an existing Firefighter qualification,

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:18.680
marked Active, with the number DEMO-CERT-1 and an expiry date.

00:00:19.129 --> 00:00:21.590
Open the intended record before changing it.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.700
An organization can use this recordkeeping pattern for its own required

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.530
qualifications, including community response, search teams, security,

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:33.450
contractor crews, and industrial response.

00:00:33.639 --> 00:00:35.939
Review the record detail before acting.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:42.259
Check the number, issuer, area, received date, expiry date, and verification date.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.999
Our example is issued by the fictional Academy Training Board.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.499
Renew has fields for a new expiry date and an optional new number.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:54.739
The continuing-education section starts with zero hours and offers

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:58.159
Hours, Date, Category, and What it was.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.729
These fields help keep an education entry attached to the correct qualification.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.130
For this software exercise, enter zero point two five hours.

00:01:07.559 --> 00:01:10.449
The Date field indicates that it defaults to today.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.100
We enter Training software demonstration as the category

00:01:14.319 --> 00:01:18.039
and a note explicitly saying that no accredited credit is claimed.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:24.320
Review the amount, date choice, category, and description before choosing Add hours.

00:01:24.699 --> 00:01:28.119
Use the actual activity information your department requires when

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:29.640
maintaining a real record.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.119
Read back the result.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:36.890
Hours added appears, the total is now zero point two five continuing-education

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.879
hours, and the stored entry includes its date, amount, category, and note.

00:01:42.289 --> 00:01:46.690
The number is still DEMO-CERT-1.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:50.130
This saved ledger distinguishes an entry that reached the

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.130
record from text left in a form.

00:01:52.569 --> 00:01:56.030
The displayed training entry is a software demonstration; its

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.870
note does not claim an accredited course or awarded qualification.

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:02.099
Next, review Renew.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:06.929
In this recorded training example, New expiry date is set to October

00:02:06.929 --> 00:02:08.649
twenty-seven, twenty twenty-eight.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.600
New number is optional and remains blank.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.439
Check the intended expiry date and whether the credential number needs

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:18.149
to change, then choose Save renewal.

00:02:18.559 --> 00:02:23.549
Keep an education-hours entry and a certification renewal distinct: one adds

00:02:23.549 --> 00:02:27.940
an activity to the ledger, while this action updates the certification record.

00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:29.780
Verify the resulting record.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:35.179
Renewal saved appears, the expiry date is October twenty-seven, twenty twenty-eight,

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.180
and the original number remains.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.899
The status now says Awaiting verification, with Not verified by the department yet.

00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:46.200
Read that state before treating the update as reviewed.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.170
The education entry remains visible below.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:54.420
This same habit supports fire and EMS personnel, community paramedicine

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.690
and mental health response teams, search and rescue, security companies,

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:03.280
wildland contractors, and industrial teams: maintain the details and

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.019
check the department review state.
